You take the rucksack off your back, and slowly sink on the ground, right on the soft underlayer of herbs. You can hardly keep your eyes open, mind clouds...
"Hey, Henry, what is wrong with you?" you hear worried voice of Conan.
"Nothing ...eh...Conan, let's rest a little. Maybe take a nap?"
"What are you talking about?! Listen, you're so pale! Henry!.."
Everything is swimming before your eyes. Like from aside you see Conan, pulling your arm, trying to pick you up. Then comes deep oblivion.


